@page "/examples/default-edge-overwrite"

<PageTitle>Default Edge Overwrite · Blow</PageTitle>

<ExampleScaffold Title="Default Edge Overwrite"
                 Summary="DefaultEdgeOptions gives every edge the user draws a house style - here an animated, round-cornered smooth step with a closed arrow, a thicker indigo stroke, a wider hit area and ends that stay put. The edge already in the list keeps the plain defaults: the options only reach new edges.">
    <ChildContent>
        <BlowCanvas Nodes="_nodes" Edges="_edges" FitViewOnInit="true" DefaultEdgeOptions="_options">
            <BlowBackground Variant="BlowBackgroundVariant.Dots" Gap="16" />
            <BlowControls />
        </BlowCanvas>
    </ChildContent>
    <TryIt>
        <li><strong>Drag</strong> from the dot under <strong>Drag from my handle</strong> to the dot on top of <strong>or here</strong>: the new edge arrives animated, smooth-stepped with round corners, indigo, thicker and with a filled arrowhead.</li>
        <li>Compare it with the grey edge into <strong>to here</strong>, which was in the list from the start and keeps the built-in look.</li>
        <li><strong>Click</strong> near the new edge rather than on it: its wider hit area still selects it.</li>
        <li>With the new edge selected no end dots appear, so its ends cannot be dragged to other handles; select the grey edge and its two dots are there to drag.</li>
        <li>Press <strong>Backspace</strong> or <strong>Delete</strong> to remove a selected edge and draw it again.</li>
    </TryIt>
    <HowItWorks>
        <li><code>DefaultEdgeOptions</code> takes a <code>BlowDefaultEdgeOptions</code>, applied to each edge the moment the user creates it; edges put in the <code>Edges</code> list by code are left alone.</li>
        <li><code>Type = SmoothStep</code> sets the path; left null it falls back to the canvas's <code>DefaultEdgeType</code>. <code>PathOptions</code> (here a <code>BorderRadius</code> of 16 instead of 5) is cloned into each new edge, so retuning one edge never retunes the others.</li>
        <li><code>Animated</code> (off by default) runs the marching dash; <code>MarkerType = ArrowClosed</code> fills the arrowhead that <code>MarkerEnd</code> (on by default) draws.</li>
        <li><code>Stroke</code> and <code>StrokeWidth</code> replace the theme colour and the 1.5 width; <code>InteractionWidth</code> widens the invisible hit path from 14 to 24 screen pixels.</li>
        <li><code>Reconnectable = false</code> (true by default) keeps new edges' ends where they were drawn. <code>Style</code>, <code>Class</code> and <code>MarkerStart</code> are there too.</li>
    </HowItWorks>
</ExampleScaffold>

@code {
    private List<BlowNode> _nodes = [];
    private List<BlowEdge> _edges = [];

    private readonly BlowDefaultEdgeOptions _options = new()
    {
        Type = BlowEdgeType.SmoothStep,
        PathOptions = new BlowEdgePathOptions { BorderRadius = 16 },
        Animated = true,
        MarkerType = BlowMarkerType.ArrowClosed,
        StrokeWidth = 2.5,
        Stroke = "#6366f1",
        InteractionWidth = 24,
        Reconnectable = false,
    };

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        _nodes =
        [
            new BlowNode { Id = "1", Type = "input", Label = "Drag from my handle", Position = new(250, 20), Width = 200 },
            new BlowNode { Id = "2", Label = "to here", Position = new(120, 170) },
            new BlowNode { Id = "3", Label = "or here", Position = new(420, 170) },
        ];
        _edges = [ new BlowEdge { Id = "e1-2", Source = "1", Target = "2" } ];
    }
}
